Fillet: a walked end cut by the face at the end runs on over the flat
stretch beyond a curved wall, not over the wall's extrapolation
(mitcad#1926).

A concave rounding along a fin's foot, its chain ending where the fin's
sloping top runs down to the plate: the fin's side is a curved wall (an
extrusion of a B-spline curve) bending tangentially into a flat stretch
(a plane) lower than the radius. The contact left the curved wall across
its edge with the top (the face at the end, holding the spine's end
vertex), and the walk ran on over the wall's surface unbounded: past the
flat stretch's edge that is the B-spline curve's polynomial
extrapolation, which bends away from the plane; the walk stopped short of
the end and WalkedCutToEnd's walk on failed the same way.

- ChFi3d_RunOnSurface (new): where N is an extrusion whose basis curve
  ends at an edge J across which a plane goes on tangentially to N, N's
  surface continued past J by the curve's tangent line (N's parameters
  kept on N), so that past J it is that plane.
- WalkedCutToEnd: with such a surface, the blend is walked again from
  the end piece's other end (as for a tight tangent face at the end) and
  cut by the face at the end from the crossing on; where the other
  contact meets the line of the edge Eq between the other face and the
  face at the end only past the spine's end vertex, on both surfaces,
  Eq is prolonged there and the face at the end grows up to the cut (as
  ChFi3d_KPartCutToEnd does); the plane, wholly under the blend, has its
  edges cut at its vertices so that the builder drops it, and its edges
  with the face at the end are passed as cut edges. Also where the walk
  ran on past the spine's end.
- PerformSetOfSurf: an end try that fails (its inner walk) no longer
  leaves the stripe failed: done is restored, as the comment there says.
- WalkedCutToEnd's pieces in the history: the walked piece that takes
  the end piece's place, and the piece cut by the face at the end, are
  faces generated by the spine's edges the end piece was (myEVIMap, as
  the other patches that replace pieces keep it); Generated() left their
  faces out, so that they had no name of their own and a later rounding
  along the top's edge with them found no edge.

